From: Sophie <ryuko@inbox.lv>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:28:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Do not grant pointer capture to fake touch apps

Apps matched by persist.waydroid.fake_touch get mouse clicks delivered
as touches. If such an app requests pointer capture (e.g. a Unity game
locking the cursor during gameplay), the mouse switches to relative
captured events, which never reach the fake touch path, and clicks stop
working.

Ignore pointer capture requests from fake touch windows so their mouse
stays absolute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java b/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java
index 8bc980c..2fda3c1 100644
--- a/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/ViewRootImpl.java
@@ -5298,6 +5298,11 @@ public final class ViewRootImpl implements ViewParent,
     }
 
     void requestPointerCapture(boolean enabled) {
+        // Fake touch turns mouse clicks into touches; a captured mouse only
+        // delivers relative motion, so those clicks would never become touches.
+        if (mFakeClickAsTouch) {
+            return;
+        }
         final IBinder inputToken = getInputToken();
         if (inputToken == null) {
             Log.e(mTag, "No input channel to request Pointer Capture.");
-- 
